{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1790931592936,"sessionID":"ses_f04290508ffeeCt1RYGZWwMNUW","part":{"id":"prt_0fbd766e6001KOLf9bE8n1i8bo","messageID":"msg_0fbd76048001bi3VbnHQo3vaaa","sessionID":"ses_f04290508ffeeCt1RYGZWwMNUW","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1790931597385,"sessionID":"ses_f04290508ffeeCt1RYGZWwMNUW","part":{"id":"prt_0fbd76792001RwAlgeKBlCEbcs","messageID":"msg_0fbd76048001bi3VbnHQo3vaaa","sessionID":"ses_f04290508ffeeCt1RYGZWwMNUW","type":"text","text":"The change is complete. Summary of what was done:\n\n- **`src/blinker/base.py`** — In `Namespace.signal`, added a guard at the top of the method: `if not isinstance(name, str): raise TypeError(...)`. This runs before the `name not in self` lookup and before any dictionary modification, so it rejects non-string names even if the namespace already contains that key.\n- Since `isinstance` is used, `str` subclasses and the empty string are accepted.\n- The module-level `signal` helper is `default_namespace.signal` (a bound method), so it inherits the same validation with no additional change.\n- The original docstring, repeated-name signal identity, `NamedSignal` naming, and receiver dispatch behavior are all untouched.","time":{"start":1790931593106,"end":1790931597377}}}
